HST Office: Alt, 2 (Alt+2) runs Undo from the quick access toolbar instead of opening its history list.

The KeyTips ran a toolbar button with ToolBox::TriggerItem, which clicks it first; a split button's click (Undo,
Redo with their ▾ history) opens its list, so Alt, 2 showed Undo's history and undid nothing (Linux and Windows,
15/11/2026). On the quick access toolbar a split button's KeyTip now dispatches the button's command, as in the
reference suite; on the ribbon a split button's KeyTip still opens its list (Alt, H, V opens Paste's menu).
The quick access KeyTips also close before their command runs, as the reference suite's do: they stayed on
after a command, so the next Alt closed them instead of showing them (Alt, 2 then Alt, 3 typed the 3).

